## Demo Scenarios

### Scenario 1: Multi-Factor Movement — Nov 2017
Select `2017-11`. Tree shows: Orders +67% (seasonal demand) BUT late deliveries 14.25% (3× normal), inventory gap 40.6% (2× normal), rating drops 3.91. Multiple interacting drivers with evidence.

### Scenario 2: Price/Competition Pressure — Aug 2018
Select `2018-08` (the last meaningful month). AOV drops 7.2%, competitor pressure index jumps to 69, competitor discounts up 3.2pp. Tree decomposes revenue change into volume vs price effects.

### Scenario 3: Abstention — Sep 2018
Select `2018-09`. Only 16 orders. Engine shows: "⛔ ABSTAIN — 16 orders vs 6,500 avg. Cannot compute reliable statistics."

### Scenario 4: Sparse History — Sep 2016
Select `2016-09`. Only 4 orders, 1 month of history. All confidence flags: "SPARSE — insufficient baseline."

### Scenario 5: Live ZIP Bulk Upload (★ Showstopper for Judges)
Judge uploads a `.zip` containing CSVs for `olist_orders`, `olist_order_items`, and `olist_order_reviews` with hypothetical Nov/Dec 2018 data. Backend auto-detects which CSV maps to which table, validates schemas, upserts ~2000 rows across 3 tables, auto-computes monthly aggregates, and renders a fresh diagnostic tree — all in one action. This proves the system handles new unseen data end-to-end.

Alternatively, they can upload a single CSV for just `bi_ai_monthly_context` with a new month row.

### Scenario 6: Persona Security
Switch COO → CMO. Freight cost, seller data, shipping_cost_index disappear from tree and narrative.

